{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:Observations.VirtualSubword","@type":"LeanModule","name":"Observations.VirtualSubword","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Units.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Powerset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Powerset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.Finset.Sigma","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":61,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_eq_zero_of_bonds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_eq_zero_of_bonds","kind":"theorem","line":410,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L410-L432","doc":"**Bond-additive set functions have no connected part beyond two parties.** Suppose that on\nevery `U ⊆ T`, `F U` is a sum of one-strand terms `g a` (for `a ∈ U`) and two-strand bond terms\n`b e` over a set `E` of two-element bonds with `e ⊆ U`. Then `connected F T = 0` whenever\n`|T| ≥ 3`. For an open chain `E` is the set of adjacent pairs, so an open chain of bonds has zero\n`n`-party connected part for every `n ≥ 3`. The bond-additivity of `F` is the input; for a\nconvolution (connected-sum) product of bonds it is the additivity of `log` of a multiplicative\ninvariant, and it is not derived here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_eq_coeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_eq_coeff","kind":"theorem","line":400,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L400-L408","doc":"**Möbius coefficient.** If `F U = ∑_{S ∈ P, S ⊆ U} w S` on every `U ⊆ T`, then the connected\npart of `F` on `T` is `w T` when `T ∈ P` and `0` otherwise. So `w` lists the genuinely\n`|S|`-party terms of `F`, and the connected part reads them off one at a time. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_weighted_contains","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_weighted_contains","kind":"theorem","line":389,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L389-L398","doc":"A weighted indicator of \"contains `S`\" has connected part `w` on `S` and `0` elsewhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_const_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_const_mul","kind":"theorem","line":382,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L382-L387","doc":"The connected part commutes with scaling. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_finset_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_finset_sum","kind":"theorem","line":375,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L375-L379","doc":"The connected part commutes with finite sums of set functions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_contains_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_contains_ne","kind":"theorem","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L352-L372","doc":"The indicator of \"contains `S`\" has zero connected part on any `T ≠ S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_contains_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_contains_self","kind":"theorem","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L339-L350","doc":"The indicator of \"contains `S`\" has connected part `1` on `S` itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_eq_zero_of_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_eq_zero_of_split","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L319-L337","doc":"**Split implies no connected part.** If `T = T₁ ∪ T₂` with `T₁, T₂` disjoint and nonempty, and\n`F` is additive over the split on every subset of `T`, then `connected F T = 0`. Contrapositive:\n`connected F T ≠ 0` means the strands of `T` do not split into two non-interacting groups. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_congr","kind":"theorem","line":312,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L312-L317","doc":"The connected part only sees the values of `F` on subsets of `T`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_add","kind":"theorem","line":306,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L306-L309","doc":"The connected part is additive in the set function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_eq_zero_of_indep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_eq_zero_of_indep","kind":"theorem","line":297,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L297-L303","doc":"A set function that ignores a strand of `T` has zero connected part on `T`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.sum_signed_eq_zero_of_indep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.sum_signed_eq_zero_of_indep","kind":"theorem","line":285,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L285-L295","doc":"If `F` does not depend on a strand `a`, the signed sum over subsets containing `a` cancels the\nsum over subsets avoiding it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected_pair","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L270-L283","doc":"On a pair the connected part is the familiar inclusion–exclusion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.connected","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.connected","kind":"def","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L266-L268","doc":"The connected part (Möbius inversion over subsets) of a set function. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.V3_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.V3_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L245-L250","doc":"**Borromean witness.** `V³` is not the identity in this representation, so `V³ ≠ 1` in `B₃`,\nalthough every pairwise cut sees cross sum `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.burau_rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.burau_rep","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L239-L243","doc":"The matrices define a representation of `B₃`: `σ₁ σ₁⁻¹ = 1` and the braid relation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.burau1i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.burau1i","kind":"def","line":236,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L236-L237","doc":"`σ₁⁻¹ ↦ [[1,0],[1,-1/t]]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.burau1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.burau1","kind":"def","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L234-L235","doc":"`σ₁ ↦ [[1,0],[t,-t]]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.burau0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.burau0","kind":"def","line":232,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L232-L233","doc":"Reduced Burau at `t = 2`: `σ₀ ↦ [[-t,1],[0,1]]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.one","kind":"def","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L229-L230","doc":"The identity matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.mul","kind":"def","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L225-L227","doc":"Matrix product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.instDecidableEqM2.decEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.instDecidableEqM2.decEq","kind":"def","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L223-L223","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.instDecidableEqM2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.instDecidableEqM2","kind":"instance","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L223-L223","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.d","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.d","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L222-L222","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.c","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.c","kind":"def","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L221-L221","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.b","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.b","kind":"def","line":220,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L220-L220","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.a","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.a","kind":"def","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L219-L219","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.M2.mk","kind":"ctor","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L218-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.M2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.M2","kind":"structure","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L217-L223","doc":"2×2 matrices over `ℚ` as four entries (enough for the witness). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.V3_pure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.V3_pure","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L213-L215","doc":"`V³` is pure: its strand permutation is the identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.V3_cross_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.V3_cross_zero","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L208-L211","doc":"Every one-strand-versus-two cut of `V³` has signed cross sum `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.V3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.V3","kind":"def","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L205-L206","doc":"The word `V³ = (σ₀ σ₁⁻¹)³`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.s1i","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.s1i","kind":"def","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L203-L204","doc":"`σ₁⁻¹` on three strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.s0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.s0","kind":"def","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L201-L202","doc":"`σ₀` on three strands. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.trivChar_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.trivChar_eq","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L176-L188","doc":"**Trivial-block shift.** A word evaluates to `q ^ writhe`, which splits into an entangled part\n`q ^ crossSum` and a self-twist part `q ^ selfSum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.trivLetter_eq_zpow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.trivLetter_eq_zpow","kind":"theorem","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L172-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.trivChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.trivChar","kind":"def","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L167-L170","doc":"Evaluation of a word in the trivial block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.trivial_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.trivial_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L162-L165","doc":"The trivial one-dimensional block satisfies the Hecke relation `(σ - q)(σ + q⁻¹) = 0`, and\n`σ⁻¹` is sent to `σ - (q - q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.trivLetter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.trivLetter","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L159-L160","doc":"The trivial block of `H_n(q)`: `σ ↦ q`, `σ⁻¹ = σ - (q - q⁻¹) ↦ q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.IsEntangledAcross","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.IsEntangledAcross","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L148-L151","doc":"A word is entangled across the cut `A | Aᶜ` when its signed cross count is nonzero (for a pure\nbraid: twice the `A`–`Aᶜ` linking number is nonzero). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.writhe_eq_cross_add_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.writhe_eq_cross_add_self","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L138-L146","doc":"Every crossing either crosses the cut or does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.writhe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.writhe","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L133-L136","doc":"The writhe: the sum of all signs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.selfSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.selfSum","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L127-L131","doc":"Signed crossings of a word between two strands on the same side of the cut. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.crossSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.crossSum","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L120-L125","doc":"Signed crossings of a word between a strand in `A` and a strand not in `A`. Positions are\ntracked from the start assignment `p`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.step","kind":"def","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L116-L118","doc":"Apply one crossing to the position→strand assignment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter.sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter.sign","kind":"def","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L113-L114","doc":"Sign of a letter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter.pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter.pos","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L111-L111","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter.adj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter.adj","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L110-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter.next","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter.next","kind":"def","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L109-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter.site","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter.site","kind":"def","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L108-L108","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter.mk","kind":"ctor","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L107-L107","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.Letter","kind":"structure","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L105-L111","doc":"A signed braid letter on `n` strands: the site `i` (crossing positions `i` and `i+1`) and the\nsign `s ∈ {+1, -1}` (`σ_i` or `σ_i⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.not_observable_of_rotation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.not_observable_of_rotation","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L92-L99","doc":"A reading of words that changes under a cyclic rotation is not an observable composed with\nevaluation. This is the abstract form of the stage-3 counterexamples. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.emit_reabsorb_isVirtual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.emit_reabsorb_isVirtual","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L88-L90","doc":"**Emission and reabsorption around the closure** is virtual for every observable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.IsVirtualLoop","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.IsVirtualLoop","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L84-L86","doc":"A split insertion: `y` is emitted before `w` and reabsorbed (`y⁻¹`) after it. It is virtual for\n`𝒪` if no member of `𝒪` sees it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.pair_isVirtual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.pair_isVirtual","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L78-L82","doc":"**Pair creation and annihilation.** `y · y⁻¹` is virtual for every family of functions,\nbecause it is already trivial in `G` (Gröbner–Shirshov null). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.observable_of_conjEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.observable_of_conjEquiv","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L73-L76","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.observable_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.observable_conj","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L67-L71","doc":"Every observable is constant on closure classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.IsVirtual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.IsVirtual","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L63-L65","doc":"A subword `x` of `u * x * v` is virtual for the family `𝒪` if inserting it changes no\nmember of `𝒪`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:virtual-subword","label":"def:virtual-subword","md":"quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.ConjEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.ConjEquiv","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L60-L61","doc":"Closure equivalence: `a` and `b` are conjugate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.VirtualSubword.IsObservable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.VirtualSubword.IsObservable","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/virtual-subword.lean#L57-L58","doc":"An observable is a class function: it cannot tell `x * y` from `y * x` (braid closure). ","signatureChunk":0}]}